% Generate `web/src/studio/Studio.jsx`: the from-scratch editing-software UI for OpenNolan (M3).
% It owns the single source-of-truth `doc` (edit_decisions), an undo/redo history, the selection +
% playhead, and the save→render-once→poll loop. EVERY edit goes through a schema-safe mutator in
% `../editor/interp.js` and flips `dirty`; Save PUTs the validated doc; Render runs the render-once
% proxy loop (only changed scenes re-render) and the preview plays the exact bytes the export
% produces (preview == export). Reuses ONLY pure, tested logic (interp.js) — no old-editor UI.
%
% Imports: `useCallback, useEffect, useMemo, useRef, useState` from 'react'; namespace `* as api`
% from '../api.js'; namespace `* as interp` from '../editor/interp.js'; `{ isFfmpeg, newTextOverlay,
% newImageOverlay, newVideoOverlay, summarizeDocChange }` from './model.js'; default `StudioToolbar`,
% `StudioTimeline`, `StudioInspector`, `StudioPreview` from their sibling files; `ChatPanel` from
% '../chat/ChatPanel.jsx'; `DebugReportModal` from './DebugReportModal.jsx'; default `dbg` from
% '../debug/recorder.js'.
%
% No inline styles except the panel-size `style={{ width|height }}` nudges called out below. Class
% names (`st-*`) are the contract with web/src/styles.css — preserve them exactly.

Default-export `Studio({ projectId, state, onClose, chat, auth, onReconnect })`.

Module constants: `POLL_MS = 500`, `POLL_MAX = 600` (~5-min ceiling); `PANELS_KEY = 'st.panels.v1'`,
`HIDDEN_KEY = 'st.hidden.v1'` (localStorage keys); panel bounds `INSPECTOR_MIN 240` (also its collapse
threshold) / `INSPECTOR_MAX 560`, `TIMELINE_MIN 150`, `TIMELINE_MAX_FRAC 0.6` (timeline ≤ 60% of the
body so the preview stays visible), `AGENT_MIN 260` / `AGENT_MAX 520`.

## State + refs
`doc` (null) mirrored synchronously by ref `docRef`; `past`/`future` ([]) undo/redo stacks; `dirty`,
`loading` (true), `loadErr` (''), `notice` (null — `{kind,msg}`). `selection` (null —
`{kind:'cut',id}` | `{kind:'overlay',index}` | `{kind:'audio',audioKind:'music'|'narration'|'sfx',
index}`); `playhead` (0, project seconds); `previewMode` ('source'|'render'); `playing` (false).
`assets` (`{kinds:{images,video,audio,music}, renders, agent_renders}` all []); `sourceMetas` ({},
ref→`{duration,width,height}`); `zoom` (80 px/s). `rendering`, `renderPath` (null), `renderVersion`
(0). Refs: `savedRef` (JSON of last-saved doc, dirty compare), `dirtyRef`/`agentBusyRef`/
`reconcilingRef` (false — closure mirrors + agent-edit guards), `jobRef` (0 — supersede in-flight poll
loops), `panelDrag` (null — active splitter teardown). Derived: `chatBusy = !!(chat && chat.busy)`,
`canvas = useMemo(interp.canvasOf(doc))`, `ffmpeg = isFfmpeg(doc)`.

`hiddenTracks` — a Set of track keys (`main`, `ov:<track>`, `aud:music|narration|sfx`) the PREVIEW
canvas skips; a per-track eye toggle, view-state only (never written to the doc, so preview==export
holds). Lazy-init from `HIDDEN_KEY` localStorage; a useEffect persists it back; `onToggleHidden(key)`
flips membership immutably. `panels` — `{inspectorW 320, timelineH 280, agentW 340, inspectorOpen,
timelineOpen, agentOpen (all true)}`, lazy-init merged over `PANELS_KEY` localStorage, persisted by a
useEffect; a cleanup useEffect runs `panelDrag.current?.()` on unmount so a splitter drag never leaks.

`flash(kind, msg)`: set notice; when kind==='ok' auto-clear after 2600ms (guarding it's still the same
msg). `dirtyRef` kept in sync with `dirty` by a useEffect.

## Transport
`togglePlay`: if starting play at/after `interp.timelineDuration(doc)` (within 1e-3) reset playhead to
0 (restart from top), then flip `playing`. `seekFromUser(t)` and `changePreviewMode(m)` both pause
(setPlaying false) then apply — a user scrub or mode switch never fights playback. All three emit a
`dbg.event`. Preview's onScrub drives the playhead during playback.

## Debug recorder
`recording = dbg.useRecording()`; `debugReport` state (null). A useEffect calls `dbg.resumeIfActive({
projectId })` (survives an accidental ⌘R). `onToggleRecord` = `dbg.toggle({ projectId, canvas:
'{w}×{h}' })`: if now recording flash a "reproduce the bug, then stop" hint; else if a session
returned, `Promise.resolve(dbg.flushed()).finally(() => setDebugReport({ session }))` so the final
batch persists before offering to send it.

## Load
useEffect on [projectId] with an `alive` guard: set loading + clear loadErr; `api.getEditDecisions`
→ use `content` or `interp.scaffoldEditDecisions({})`, write docRef+doc+savedRef, `setDirty(!content)`
(a scaffold is unsaved), and select the first cut if any; catch → loadErr = message; finally clear
loading. Also `api.listAssets` → setAssets (ignore errors). A second useEffect on [doc, projectId,
sourceMetas] lazily probes `api.getSourceMeta` for each distinct non-empty `c.source` not yet in
sourceMetas (storing null on error), for trim bounds + scrub.

## History / mutation
INVARIANT: never nest a setState inside another setState updater (StrictMode double-invokes updaters
in dev → nested setters corrupt the stacks). `setDocBoth(nd)` writes docRef then setDoc. `snapshot()`
pushes `docRef.current` onto `past` (slice to last 100) and clears `future` WITHOUT changing the doc —
called once at a coalesced drag's start so the whole drag is one undo step. `live(next)` (accepts a
value or updater of docRef.current): referential no-op returns early; else emit `dbg.event('edit.live',
summarizeDocChange(prev,nd))`, setDocBoth, setDirty(true) — NO history (per-frame drag). `commit(next)`
= discrete edit: same no-op guard, emit `edit.commit`, push prev onto past (cap 100) + clear future,
setDocBoth, dirty. `undo`/`redo` move the top item between the stacks, setDocBoth, dirty, emit
`edit.undo`/`edit.redo`; each reads the latest `past`/`future` from its closure deps.

## Save / autosave / render
`persist({silent})` (async, reads docRef so it always writes the LATEST doc): bail if no doc; if
`agentBusyRef` or `reconcilingRef` is set, log a blocked event and (unless silent) warn "Agent is
editing — your changes will save the moment its turn ends", return null — never clobber the agent's
write. Else `api.saveEditDecisions`, update savedRef, clear dirty, flash 'Saved' unless silent, return
the doc; on throw flash `Save rejected: {msg}` unless silent, return null. `save = persist({silent:
false})`. `flushAutosave` = if dirtyRef, `persist({silent:true})`. Autosave useEffect on [dirty, doc,
chatBusy]: when dirty and NOT (chatBusy || agentBusyRef || reconcilingRef), a 700ms debounced
`persist({silent:true})` (cleared on change) — the on-disk edit_decisions.json is the source of truth
shared with the agent, so keep it current; suspended during/around an agent turn.

`chatForPanel = useMemo`: if chat, spread it and wrap only `send` so it `await flushAutosave()` before
`chat.send(text)` (hand the agent our latest timeline, not a stale disk copy); else pass chat through.

`render` (async): return if rendering; `await save()` first and abort if it returned falsy (always
render the SAVED doc). Set rendering, flash "Rendering… (only changed scenes re-render)", claim
`myJob = ++jobRef.current`. `api.startRender` → poll up to POLL_MAX times: bail if `jobRef.current !==
myJob` (superseded); sleep POLL_MS; `api.getRenderStatus` — on 'done' set renderPath=output_path, bump
renderVersion, switch previewMode to 'render', flash 'Rendered' (append ` — {warnings joined by ' · '}`
when present); on 'failed' flash `Render failed: {error||'unknown'}`; each branch logs a `ui.render`
phase and returns. After the loop flash 'Render timed out'. Catch → flash `Render error: {msg}`.
Finally, only clear rendering if this is still the current job.

## Agent reconcile (shared source of truth)
The in-editor agent shares the project conversation, so it can rewrite edit_decisions.json on disk
while the editor holds an open-time snapshot. useEffect on [chatBusy, projectId, flash]: read the
previous busy from `agentBusyRef`, then set `agentBusyRef.current = chatBusy`; act only on a turn that
JUST ended (was busy, now not) with a projectId. Open `reconcilingRef` (held across the async refetch
so an autosave/Save can't race it). Refresh `api.listAssets` (the agent may have rendered new clips).
`api.getEditDecisions` → if content and its JSON differs from savedRef: note `hadLocal =
dirtyRef.current`, log `agent.adopt`, and if hadLocal push the user's mid-turn doc onto `past` (cap
100) + clear future so ⌘Z restores it; then adopt the agent's doc LIVE (docRef+doc+savedRef, clear
dirty) and flash "Timeline updated by the agent" (append " — ⌘Z to restore your version" when
hadLocal). Finally clear `reconcilingRef`.

## Selection-aware handlers
Derive `selCut` (the selected cut), `selOverlayIndex` (-1 when none), `selAudio` (the audio selection
or null), and `selAudioObj` — `interp.musicRegions(doc)[i]` for music, `doc.audio.narration.segments[i]`
for narration, else `doc.audio.sfx[i]`. Trim uses the live/snapshot pattern: `onTrimBegin = snapshot`;
`onTrim(cutId, patch)` looks up the cut's source meta and `live(interp.trimCut(d, cutId, patch, {
sourceDuration }))`. `onSplit` acts on whatever is selected at the playhead — overlay
(`splitOverlay`), music (`splitMusic`), narration (`splitNarration`), sfx (warn "a single cue —
nothing to split"), else the main cut (`splitCutAtPlayhead`); the pure mutator returns the same ref
when the playhead isn't strictly inside, which we surface as a per-kind "move the playhead inside…"
warn; otherwise `commit`. `onDelete` removes the selected cut/overlay/audio via the matching interp
remover and clears selection — but refuse (warn "Can't delete the last clip") when it's the only cut.
`onDuplicate` = `interp.duplicateCut` on the selected cut. `onReorder(from,to)` = `interp.reorderCut`.

## Add handlers (Assets click / drag-drop) + audio editing
`onAddClip(path, atTime)`: default out = min(meta.duration, 8) or 5; when atTime is given, insert
before/after the cut under the drop (`interp.cutAtTime`, split at its midpoint); `commit(interp.addCut(
…, atIndex))`. `onSetMusic(path)` = `interp.setMusic` (flash 'Music set'). `onAddMusic(path, atTime)`:
first bed (no music regions) → setMusic; else a bounded region at atTime-or-playhead spanning
min(meta.duration, 30)|12s (flash 'Music region added'). `onAddSfx(path, atTime)` = `interp.addSfx` at
atTime-or-playhead. `onUpdateAudio(patch)` / `onLiveUpdateAudio(patch)` edit the SELECTED audio item
(music/narration/sfx via the matching interp updater) through commit / live respectively.

Overlay adds auto-pick a track via `interp.placeOverlayTrack(d, start, end, preferredTrack)` (interval
partitioning — a would-overlap overlay lands on its own new lane so both stay visible), then select
the new overlay by index: `onAddText` (2.5s at the playhead, clamped), `onAddImage(assetId, atTime,
track=0)` (3s), `onAddVideoOverlay(assetId, atTime, track=0)` (min(meta.duration,6)|4s). `onAutoArrange`
= `interp.autoArrangeOverlays(docRef.current)`; commit unless it no-ops (then flash "already
arranged"). `onAssetDrop(kind, path, t, target={})` routes by target: music→onAddMusic, audio→onAddSfx,
`lane==='cuts'`→onAddClip (main clip), video→onAddVideoOverlay, else onAddImage — declared AFTER the
add-handlers it calls so they aren't read in their temporal dead zone (a TDZ ReferenceError here
crashes the whole editor on mount, which the build can't catch).

Timeline drags use the snapshot-once/live pattern (`onOverlayDragBegin`/`onAudioDragBegin` =
snapshot): `onOverlayMove`/`onOverlayTrim` (interp move/trimOverlay), `onOverlayResolve` (float off a
new same-track overlap via `resolveOverlayOverlap` — `live` folds it into the drag's one undo step);
audio `onMoveSfx`/`onMoveNarration`/`onTrimNarration` and music `onSetMusicLive`/`onTrimMusic`/
`onMoveMusic`, each targeting an explicit index (unlike the selection-based onUpdateAudio). Canvas
drags (also `live`): `onOverlayPosition(index, xy)` merges rounded `{x,y}` into the overlay's position
object (converting a text-anchor string to an object on first drag); `onClipPosition(cutId, xy)` merges
into `transform.position` preserving scale/crop; `onClipDragBegin = snapshot`. `onSelectOverlay(index)`
selects the overlay. `onNormalizeOverlay(index, patch)` = `interp.updateOverlay` through `live` (NOT
commit) so self-healing an agent-authored string-anchor image/video overlay on mere SELECTION never
pushes a phantom undo step.

## Remaining handlers
`onSetBackground` (`interp.setBackground`), `onCanvas({width,height})` (`interp.setCanvas`),
`onUpdateCut`/`onUpdateOverlay` (commit) with `onLiveUpdateCut`/`onLiveUpdateOverlay` (live, for
scrub-field drags where `onScrubBegin = snapshot` opens one undo step), and keyframe
`onSetKeyframes`/`onUpsertKeyframe`/`onRemoveKeyframe` (commit). `refreshAssets` re-lists;
`onUploadAsset(kind, file)` = `api.uploadAsset` then refreshAssets + flash (log a `ui.uploadAsset`
event either way).

`beginPanelDrag(e, axis)`: preventDefault, capture start x/y + panel sizes + the `.st-body`
clientHeight; one pointerdown→window pointermove/up/cancel model (same as the timeline), storing the
teardown in `panelDrag.current`. axis `'agent'`: width = start + Δx (handle sits right of the panel),
collapse below AGENT_MIN else clamp to AGENT_MAX. axis `'x'`: inspector width = start + (startX − x)
(drag left = wider), collapse below INSPECTOR_MIN else clamp INSPECTOR_MAX. axis `'y'`: timeline
height = start + (startY − y) (drag up = taller), collapse below TIMELINE_MIN else clamp to
max(TIMELINE_MIN, bodyH × TIMELINE_MAX_FRAC).

## Effects: selection cleanup, select logging, keyboard
- On [doc, selection]: clear a selection whose overlay index or audio item no longer exists (so the
  inspector never edits a phantom index).
- On [selection]: emit a `dbg.event('ui.select', …)` for the trace.
- On [undo, redo, save, onSplit, onDelete]: a window keydown. Ignore while a field is focused
  (INPUT/TEXTAREA/SELECT/isContentEditable) OR a `role="slider"` scrub bar is focused (it owns those
  keys). Space = play/pause (preventDefault, toggle `playing`); Escape = clear selection; ⌘/Ctrl+Z =
  undo (Shift = redo); ⌘/Ctrl+S = save; bare `s`/`S` = onSplit; Delete/Backspace = onDelete — each
  preventDefault.

## Render
While loading: `st` > `st-loading` "Loading timeline…". On loadErr: an `st` with an `st-bar` back
button (`st-ghost` "← Back" → onClose) and an `st-loading st-err-text` "Couldn't load: {loadErr}".
Otherwise compute `dur = interp.timelineDuration(doc)` and render `st`:
- `st-bar`: an `st-bar-left` with a `st-ghost` "←" (title "Back to project" → onClose), an `st-title`
  (`state?.name || projectId`), and an `st-dirty` "● unsaved" when dirty; then `<StudioToolbar>`
  passed doc/canvas/ffmpeg, canUndo/canRedo (stack lengths), dirty/rendering/`hasRender`
  (`!!renderPath`)/previewMode, and onUndo/onRedo/onSave/onRender/onPreviewMode(changePreviewMode)/
  onAddText/onCanvas plus recording/onToggleRecord.
- When NOT ffmpeg, an `st-banner` noting this timeline's runtime is `doc.render_runtime` and the studio
  targets the FFmpeg render path. `notice` → an `st-notice {kind}` with its msg.
- `st-body` > `st-body-top`: when `chat`, either (agentOpen) an `st-agent-wrap` (style width
  panels.agentW) holding `<ChatPanel chat={chatForPanel} disabled={!projectId} className="st-agent"
  auth onReconnect />` followed by an `st-vsplit` splitter (onPointerDown beginPanelDrag 'agent'), or
  (collapsed) an `st-reopen st-reopen-v st-reopen-agent` "›" button that reopens the agent panel.
  Then `<StudioPreview>` (projectId/doc/canvas/playhead/previewMode/renderPath/renderVersion/playing/
  selection/sourceMetas, `hidden={hiddenTracks}`, onScrub=setPlayhead, onPlayingChange=setPlaying,
  onSelectOverlay/onOverlayPosition/onOverlayDragBegin, onClipPosition, `onClipDragBegin={snapshot}`).
  Then the inspector: when inspectorOpen, an `st-vsplit` (beginPanelDrag 'x') + an `st-inspector-wrap`
  (style width panels.inspectorW) holding `<StudioInspector>` (projectId/doc/canvas/ffmpeg, selCut/
  selOverlayIndex/playhead/selAudio/selAudioObj, assets/sourceMetas, and the update/live/keyframe/add/
  background/upload handlers, `onScrubBegin={snapshot}`); else an `st-reopen st-reopen-v` "‹" reopen
  button.
- Below `st-body-top`, when timelineOpen: an `st-hsplit` (beginPanelDrag 'y') + an `st-timeline-wrap`
  (style height panels.timelineH) holding `<StudioTimeline>` (projectId/doc/dur/zoom/playhead/
  selection/sourceMetas/playing, onSeek=seekFromUser, onSelect=setSelection, and the trim/reorder/
  zoom/assetDrop/overlay-drag/audio-drag/music handlers, hidden/onToggleHidden, plus onTogglePlay/
  onSplit/onDuplicate/onDelete/onAutoArrange); else an `st-reopen st-reopen-h` "Timeline ▴" reopen
  button. Each reopen button restores its panel to at least its MIN size.
- Finally, when `debugReport`, a `<DebugReportModal session={debugReport.session} onClose={() =>
  setDebugReport(null)} />`.
